       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg per dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risk:** At this dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours:** typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg total per day,** divided into smaller doses, such as 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intended and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
